{
  "ticket": "Good morning, Northbeam Support team, I hope you are having a productive week. I am writing to urgently report that as of approximately 08:45 AM EST this morning, our entire project management team of twelve engineers and site supervisors has been completely unable to access the Northbeam dashboard; we are all encountering a persistent '503 Service Unavailable' error when attempting to load the login page or any internal URLs, and our API integration with our field reporting tools has also started returning 502 Bad Gateway responses, which effectively halts our ability to track daily progress reports for the three active construction sites we are managing simultaneously. We have verified that our own internet connections are stable and that our local firewalls have not blocked any Northbeam IP addresses, and several team members have confirmed that they are seeing the exact same error messages on their respective devices, indicating this is a widespread service issue rather than a local configuration problem. Since no member of our organization can log in or retrieve data, we are currently unable to submit mandatory daily logs or update task statuses, which is causing immediate delays in our weekly compliance reporting, and we would greatly appreciate it if you could investigate this outage immediately as we are losing critical operational visibility. Please let us know if there is any additional information or diagnostic logs you need from our end to help expedite the restoration of service for our whole team.",
  "category": "outage",
  "priority": "P1",
  "rationale": "The ticket describes a whole-team service unavailability where the login page and API are returning errors for everyone, which classifies as an outage and is assigned P1 priority because all outage tickets are P1."
}

