{
  "ticket": "Hi there, it's Martha from the accounting department here, and I know it's the middle of the month so I'm sure you're swamped, but I just needed to clear some space on my personal laptop because it's getting so sluggish and I think my old hard drive is failing, which is a whole other story involving my cat knocking over a glass of water last Tuesday and shorting out my mouse, which I'm still trying to dry out with rice as you can imagine is very stressful for a small business owner who has to file taxes by Friday and doesn't have time for IT dramas, but anyway, while I was trying to clean up some files to make room for the new quarterly reports, I realized I had an old sandbox account we used for testing the integration back in 2021 before we went live with the main company profile, and I don't actually need that data anymore since we've been using the real system for three years, but I'm not entirely sure if clicking 'delete' on the dashboard actually purges everything from your servers permanently or if it just hides it from view for a while, and since I'm responsible for GDPR compliance in our office and we had a few clients from the EU back in those early pilot days, I want to be absolutely certain that all personal data associated with that specific user profile is completely erased from your systems to avoid any potential liability down the road, so could you please initiate a full data deletion for that old account? Also, my coffee machine has been making a weird grinding noise lately which might mean the grinder is broken but I haven't had time to call the repair guy yet.",
  "category": "data_request",
  "priority": "P3",
  "rationale": "The dominant issue is a request to delete all data associated with a user profile, which falls under data_request, and per policy, all data_request tickets are assigned priority P3."
}

{
  "ticket": "Hello Northbeam Support team, I hope this message finds you well. I am the office manager at Bright Smile Dental and I am writing to report a critical issue that has come up this morning which is preventing our entire administrative staff from completing their daily workflow. Specifically, the patient scheduling board is displaying incorrect availability times that do not match our actual calendar slots, causing us to accidentally double-book three patients for procedures that are already scheduled. We have attempted to refresh the page, clear our browser cache, and even tried accessing the system from a different computer in the lobby, but the data remains persisted incorrectly across all devices. This is not merely a visual glitch because when we try to manually override the slots to fix the error, the 'Save' button fails to process and returns a silent error without updating the database, meaning we cannot create or modify appointments at all. Our front desk is currently unable to check patients in or schedule future visits, which is causing a significant bottleneck as we are seeing patients in the operatories right now who cannot be properly checked in. There is absolutely no workaround for this situation since we cannot manually track these appointments in a separate system due to compliance requirements with our practice management software integration, and we need this resolved as soon as possible to avoid turning away walk-in patients today. Thank you for your assistance.",
  "category": "technical_issue",
  "priority": "P2",
  "rationale": "The ticket describes a product malfunction (scheduling board data errors and save failures) while the service is generally up, and the customer explicitly states that work is blocked with no workaround, which maps to P2 under the technical_issue category rules."
}

