{
  "ticket": "Hi there, this is Marcus from the Riverside Community Outreach Center, and I’m writing to you because our executive director, Brenda, was just telling me how stressful the last quarter has been with the grant reporting deadline looming and our server room being basically a glorified closet that smells like old coffee and desperation, and while we appreciate Northbeam helping us track our volunteer hours, I am currently facing a bit of a bureaucratic nightmare regarding our data privacy compliance for the new state nonprofit regulations. See, I was digging through our records yesterday, maybe around the time I was trying to reconcile invoice #NB-99284-KL which seemed to have some weird line items for 'premium support' that I definitely didn't authorize, but that's not the main point right now because our legal counsel is breathing down my neck about GDPR and CCPA compliance for our donors, and they specifically asked me to get an official export of all personally identifiable information stored by Northbeam for our entire organization, including the donor contact lists, transaction histories, and any notes attached to those records, so that we can properly archive them and ensure we are meeting the statutory retention requirements before we potentially switch vendors or just go cold turkey next year. I know this sounds like a hassle and I know Brenda usually handles the emails but she’s currently at a fundraising gala so I’m just trying to get this done ASAP so I can show the board that we are being proactive about data stewardship, even though our current software setup is a bit of a Frankenstein monster of spreadsheets and this app, but please just send me the complete data dump for our account associated with the email admin@riversideoutreach.org so I can pass it to our compliance officer.",
